<content><![CDATA[<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>
<multiple-choice question="What is the main benefit of building an environment from a modular kit?" single-option="" randomize="">
  <input type="checkbox" value="Pieces can be reused and snapped together to build many layouts efficiently" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="Every piece needs its own unique texture">
  <input type="checkbox" value="It removes the need for level design">
  <input type="checkbox" value="It increases draw calls, which improves quality">
</multiple-choice>
<true-false-question question="Modular pieces are easier to assemble when they are built to a consistent grid size.">
  <input type="checkbox" value="True" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="False">
</true-false-question>
<self-check title="Think it through">
  <p slot="question">How can lighting and landmarks guide a player through an environment?</p>
  <p>Brighter or contrasting light and color draw the eye toward the path, framing and leading lines point the way, and distinctive landmarks visible from a distance help players keep their bearings.</p>
</self-check>
